  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"157\" data-end=\"349\">The <strong data-start=\"161\" data-end=\"192\">Arylsulfatase A (ARSA) test</strong> measures the activity of the <strong data-start=\"222\" data-end=\"237\">ARSA enzyme</strong>, which plays a critical role in the breakdown of <strong data-start=\"287\" data-end=\"301\">sulfatides</strong>, a type of lipid found in the nervous system.</p>\n<p data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"384\">This test is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"385\" data-end=\"755\">\n<li data-start=\"385\" data-end=\"475\">\n<p data-start=\"387\" data-end=\"475\">Diagnose <strong data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"434\">Metachromatic Leukodystrophy (MLD)</strong>, a rare <strong data-start=\"443\" data-end=\"473\">lysosomal storage disorder</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"476\" data-end=\"560\">\n<p data-start=\"478\" data-end=\"560\">Differentiate <strong data-start=\"492\" data-end=\"499\">MLD</strong> from other leukodystrophies or neurodegenerative disorders</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"561\" data-end=\"661\">\n<p data-start=\"563\" data-end=\"661\">Identify <strong data-start=\"572\" data-end=\"597\">ARSA pseudodeficiency</strong> in some individuals with reduced enzyme levels but no disease</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"755\">\n<p data-start=\"664\" data-end=\"755\">Guide <strong data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"689\">carrier testing</strong> and <strong data-start=\"694\" data-end=\"716\">prenatal diagnosis</strong> in families with known MLD mutations</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"757\" data-end=\"917\">MLD leads to progressive <strong data-start=\"782\" data-end=\"799\">demyelination</strong> of the central and peripheral nervous systems, with symptoms such as motor regression, ataxia, and cognitive decline.</p>\n<p data-start=\"757\" data-end=\"917\">&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Metachromatic Leukodystrophy (MLD)</strong></td>\n<td>Caused by ARSA deficiency &rarr; sulfatide accumulation &rarr; progressive neurodegeneration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ARSA pseudodeficiency</strong></td>\n<td>Reduced enzyme activity but no clinical symptoms; important to distinguish from true MLD</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Carrier state</strong></td>\n<td>Heterozygous individuals may show mild reduction; no disease but relevant for genetic counseling</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"757\" data-end=\"917\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p data-start=\"1657\" data-end=\"1855\">A diagnosis of MLD is <strong data-start=\"1679\" data-end=\"1692\">confirmed</strong> by <strong data-start=\"1696\" data-end=\"1712\">enzyme assay</strong>, and often <strong data-start=\"1724\" data-end=\"1743\">genetic testing</strong> is done to identify mutations in the <strong data-start=\"1781\" data-end=\"1794\">ARSA gene</strong>. <strong data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1823\">Urine sulfatide testing</strong> may also support the diagnosis.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"1857\" data-end=\"1860\">\n<p data-start=\"1862\" data-end=\"1997\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">&nbsp;</p>",
